  "version": 5,
  "description": "Products in scope. Tier 1 is interrupt-eligible; tier 2 is feed only and never posts critical. Items outside both tiers do not post. match: exact identities, lowercase and trimmed. A product text resolves to an entry only when the whole text, NFKC-normalised, lowercased, with Unicode dashes as '-' and whitespace runs as one space, equals one identity; nothing is matched by a word, a prefix or a substring, so claude-code-router is not Claude Code. An identity is a product name, a repository slug (owner/repo), a package key (ecosystem:name, the form a collector finding's package field takes) or CISA KEV's vendorProject and product joined by one space. Each identity belongs to one entry or component in the whole file. components (optional): a list of {name, match, authority?}, each a public product identity a member's inventory can report; a text that equals a component's identity resolves to that component, which is the product a post names, its upgrade target and its thread key. An entry has match, components or both. Entry and component names are unique across the file; a component may carry its own entry's name. authority (optional, on an entry or a component; a component's list replaces its entry's, and an empty list means none): URL prefixes, host/ or host/path/, lowercase, where that product's own vendor publishes advisories; a github.com prefix names one repository (github.com/owner/repo/), never an owner. A source is authoritative for a product only when it is on spec/primary-domains.json and under one of these prefixes; the CISA KEV catalog the poster fetched is authoritative for any product. A product with no authority posts from KEV only. Version 5 is the only version a reader accepts.",
